@startuml
title Aveli — Product Boundary

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontColor black
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  FontColor black
  RoundCorner 8
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  FontColor black
}
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ActorBorderColor black
skinparam ActorFontColor black

left to right direction

actor "Independent\nSpecialist" as User

package "Aveli" as Aveli {
  rectangle "Professional Workspace\n\nClients\nAppointments & Visits\nServices\nPayments\nNotes & Photos\nToday & Calendar\nSchedule & Preferences" as Workspace

  rectangle "Account & Access\n\nRegistration & Sign-in\nTrial\nSubscription Access\nManual Access\nLifetime Access\nAccess Restoration" as Access
}

rectangle "Mobile Platform\nBilling" as Billing
rectangle "Device Contacts" as Contacts
rectangle "Device Notifications" as Notifications
rectangle "Exchange-rate Source" as Rates

rectangle "Out of Current Scope\n\nShared team workspace\nMulti-device workspace sync\nPublic online booking\nEnterprise CRM\nFull accounting\nOrganization management" as OutOfScope

User --> Workspace : daily professional work
User --> Access : identity & access

Access ..> Billing : subscription / restore
Workspace ..> Contacts : optional contact import
Workspace ..> Notifications : appointment reminders
Workspace ..> Rates : supported currency context

Aveli ..> OutOfScope : intentionally excluded

note bottom of Aveli
The diagram defines product responsibility.
It does not describe implementation technologies.
end note

@enduml
